   <caption unique="1092335">Instruction Operand Encoding</caption>
   </table>
  </operand_table>
 <longdesc><para unique="1092337">URDMSR reads the contents of a 64-bit MSR specified in operand 2 into operand 1. Operand 1 is a general-purpose register, while operand 2 may be either a general-purpose register or an immediate. URDMSR reads the indicated MSR in the same manner as RDMSR.</para>
  <para unique="1092338">MSRs readable by RDMSR with CPL = 0 can be read by URDMSR at any privilege level but under OS control. The OS controls what MSRs can be read by the URDMSR and UWRMSR instructions with a 4-KByte <bold>user-MSR bitmap</bold> located at an aligned linear address in the IA32_USER_MSR_CTL MSR (address 1CH). The URDMSR instruction is enabled only if bit 0 of this MSR is 1.</para>
  <para unique="1092339">The low 2 KBytes of the bitmap control URDMSR (they compose the URDMSR bitmap); these 2 KBytes include one bit for each MSR address in the range 0H&#8211;3FFFH. URDMSR may read an MSR only if the bit corresponding to the MSR has value 1; otherwise (or if the MSR address is outside that range) URDMSR causes a general-protection exception (#GP).</para>
  <para unique="1092340">The URDMSR accesses to these bitmaps are implicit supervisor-mode accesses, which means they use supervisor privilege regardless of CPL. <anchor id="+314073"/></para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <programlisting>DEST := MSR[SRC]</programlisting>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1092386">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Protected Mode Exceptions">
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term>#UD</term>
    <listitem><para unique="1092388">The URDMSR instruction is not recognized outside 64-bit mode.</para>
     </listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Real-Address Mode Exceptions">
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term>#UD</term>
    <listitem><para unique="1092390">The URDMSR instruction is not recognized outside 64-bit mode.</para>
     </listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Virtual-8086 Mode Exceptions">
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term>#UD</term>
    <listitem><para unique="1092392">The URDMSR instruction is not recognized outside 64-bit mode.</para>
     </listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Compatibility Mode Exceptions">
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term>#UD</term>
    <listitem><para unique="1092394">The URDMSR instruction is not recognized outside 64-bit mode.</para>
     </listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="64-Bit Mode Exceptions">
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term>#GP(0)</term>
    <listitem><para unique="1092396">If MSR_address[63:14] is not all zero.</para>
     </listitem>
    <listitem><para unique="1092397">If the MSR address is in the range 0&#8722;3FFH and bit n in the URDMSR bitmap is 0, where n is the MSR address.</para>
     </listitem>
    <listitem><para unique="1092398">If RDMSR from the specified MSR would result in a #GP(0) exception due to the MSR not being accessible.</para>
     </listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term>#UD </term>
    <listitem><para unique="1092400">If the LOCK prefix is used.</para>
     </listitem>
    <listitem><para unique="1092401">If CPUID.07H.01H:EDX.USER_MSR[15] = 0.</para>
     </listitem>
    <listitem><para unique="1092402">If IA32_USER_MSR_CTL.ENABLE = 0.</para>
     </listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
